{"call_id":"7c08f54b-561a-41d7-ae9d-91c4f6aa809c","metadata":{"error_type":null,"finish_reason":"stop","mode":"ok","response_id":"ed7b1850460ac6381e94bfb088c82c4f.243a135bf417a401f4e9dcbcb07d18c5","status_code":null,"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"cached_tokens":4096,"completion_tokens":1822,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":0,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":null},"prompt_tokens":5102,"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cache_write_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":4096,"image_tokens":null,"text_tokens":null},"total_tokens":6924}},"raw_response":{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null,"message":{"annotations":null,"audio":null,"content":"{\n  \"protocol_version\": \"impact-response-v3\",\n  \"action\": \"read\",\n  \"summary\": \"当前单元为 normalized:1 (D4)，fixed_text_evidence 为空，无法提供文档引用。请求读取主差异 D4 及两个解析片段 P1/P2，以获取真实原文位置与哈希绑定后再进行规则发现。\",\n  \"reads\": {\n    \"difference_refs\": [\n      \"D4\"\n    ],\n    \"segment_refs\": [\n      \"P1\",\n      \"P2\"\n    ]\n  }\n}","function_call":null,"reasoning":"The user wants me to analyze document impact based on fixed evidence. I need to return an impact-response-v3 JSON object.\n\nLet me analyze the current state:\n- Stage is \"discover_rules\"\n- rules is empty []\n- I need to discover rules from the fixed text evidence\n- The primary difference is \"normalized:1\" (D4)\n- There's an insert operation in the new document: \"\\r\\n## 订单导出\\r\\n新增GET /orders/export，导出订单按创建时间倒序排列。\\r\\n\"\n- Old text at end_char 126 is empty\n- New source has sections including \"订单导出\" at end_char 139\n- Old source has sections ending at 126\n\nThe difference shows a new section \"订单导出\" with text \"新增GET /orders/export，导出订单按创建时间倒序排列。\"\n\nBut wait, the fixed_text_evidence is empty {}. The instruction says \"In discovery, document_citations is a list of T references from fixed_text_evidence\". But fixed_text_evidence is empty.\n\nLet me re-read... The coordination context says discovery_units is empty, rules is empty, stage is discover_rules.\n\nSince fixed_text_evidence is empty, and the primary difference contains the actual text directly, I could use the primary difference to identify the rule. But document_citations must be T references from fixed_text_evidence. Since there are no T references, and I cannot calculate offsets or quotes, I may need to request reads.\n\nWait, the protocol says: \"In discovery, document_citations is a list of T references from fixed_text_evidence; select supplied original text, never calculate/copy offsets, quotes, UUIDs or hashes.\"\n\nBut fixed_text_evidence is empty. I need to request reads to get the text evidence. The primary difference contains the text inline though. However, the schema wants T references for document citations.\n\nActually, looking at the primary difference, it's provided directly in the JSON. But the analysis_protocol says document_citations must be T references from fixed_text_evidence. Since fixed_text_evidence is empty, I should request reads first.\n\nThe action should be \"read\" to get the evidence I need. I need to read the differences and segments to get proper T references.\n\nWait, I need to check if there's more context. The primary difference is given, but I need to request the fixed text evidence to cite it properly. The instruction says \"Request fixed reads for missing/cross-section evidence.\"\n\nSince fixed_text_evidence is empty, I need to make read requests. I can request:\n- difference_refs for D4 to get the text evidence\n- Maybe segment refs P1, P2 to get the parsed content\n\nActually, looking at the structure, fixed_text_evidence seems to be something the server will load when I request reads. So I should request reads first.\n\nLet me propose a read request for the difference D4 (normalized:1) and possibly segments to understand context.\n\nThe response schema for BoundReadRequest includes:\n- case_refs\n- difference_refs\n- ranges\n- segment_refs\n\nI'll request the difference_refs for D4 and maybe D1-D6 to understand all differences, and segments P1/P2.\n\nBut wait, the user message shows the primary difference already. However, the analysis requires citations as T references. Since fixed_text_evidence is empty, I must request reads.\n\nLet me craft the read request. I'll ask for all differences D1-D6 and segments P1-P2.\n\nActually, the primary unit is normalized:1 which is D4. But to understand the full context, especially the old vs new document, I should read the sources. Segments P1 and P2 are available.\n\nLet me request:\n- difference_refs: [\"D1\", \"D2\", \"D3\", \"D4\", \"D5\", \"D6\"] (or just D4)\n- segment_refs: [\"P1\", \"P2\"]\n\nThe protocol says: \"Use short S/P/C/D references for reads.\"\n\nI think requesting D4, P1, P2 would be good. But D4 is the primary. However, to understand if there are cross-section changes, I might need all. But the primary difference contains the insert.\n\nActually, the primary field already shows the exact difference. But fixed_text_evidence is needed for citations. Let me just request the relevant reads.\n\nThe response schema requires for action=read: summary, protocol_version, action, reads. No candidates or unit_outcome.\n\nLet me make the read request:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"protocol_version\": \"impact-response-v3\",\n  \"action\": \"read\",\n  \"summary\": \"Requesting fixed text evidence for the inserted 订单导出 section in normalized:1 and the corresponding source segments to anchor rule discovery.\",\n  \"reads\": {\n    \"difference_refs\": [\"D4\"],\n    \"segment_refs\": [\"P1\", \"P2\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWait, but I should check if D4 maps to primary_ref. Yes, primary_ref is \"D4\".\n\nHowever, I also see there are other differences: D1 (raw:0), D2 (raw:1), D3 (normalized:0), D5 (section:0), D6 (section:1). Since I'm in discovery for unit normalized:1 (D4), and the primary difference already contains the text, requesting